# Orca copies these ignored paths from the primary checkout when it creates a
# worktree. Keep entries literal: globs and negation are not supported.
#
# Two things this does NOT do, both worth knowing:
#
#   - It copies at creation time and does not backfill. Worktrees that already
#     exist keep whatever they had; recreate them, or copy the file in once.
#   - The copies are independent. Rotating a key in the primary checkout does
#     not update any worktree, and a stale copy fails in ways that look like
#     application bugs rather than configuration ones. Resync after rotating.

# Local development environment. Without this, a fresh worktree has no Supabase
# URL or keys and every authed page throws on the service-role client.
.env.local

# Preserves the Vercel project link so `vercel` commands and the sandbox
# snapshot script work in a worktree without running `vercel link` again.
.vercel
